# Build context for the two images built from the repository root: the app
# (Dockerfile) and the daily backup (backup/Dockerfile). Both copy only
# requirements.txt, web/, gunicorn.conf.py and three files of scripts/ — a few
# megabytes out of half a gigabyte of context. Everything below is either a
# secret, a copy of the same file git already keeps, or a tool's local state.
#
# The other three services build from their own folder (compose sets context
# to ./frontend, ./nginx and ./mcp), so what is listed here does not touch them.

# Version history, 57 MB, and it holds every past version of every file.
.git

# Secrets. The images take no .env (compose passes the values as environment),
# but the context is uploaded to the daemon and kept in the build cache.
.env
.env.*

# Local state of the tools, and the virtualenv the stand runs on (458 MB).
.venv
venv/
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Dependencies and build output of the frontend. It is its own build context
# and the Python images copy nothing from it.
frontend/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Not part of any image: the source of the other services (own contexts), the
# tests and the checks, and what they leave behind.
nginx/
mcp/
tests/
e2e/
docs/
audit/
screenshots/
*.log

# Tool state and agent instructions at the root.
.githooks/
.github/
.claude/
.impeccable/

# One-off check scripts write their screenshots into the root (see .gitignore).
/*.png